# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
config RUST_X86_E820
	bool "Rust x86-64 E820 memory map owner"
	depends on RUST && X86_64
	default y
	help
	  Use the Rust implementation for the canonical e820.o archive entry.
	  Rust owns map queries, sanitation, mutation, PCI gap selection, boot
	  parameter parsing, firmware ingestion, resources and memblock setup.
	  Configured native headers provide types, constants and provider ABIs.
	  Only BUG, the fixed LA57 CPU-feature compiler predicate, kmemdup's
	  allocation compiler macros and initcall/export metadata use C glue.
	  GCC_PLUGIN_LATENT_ENTROPY and KSTACK_ERASE currently cause explicit
	  errors because their instrumentation parity has not been implemented.
	  The original e820.c remains unchanged.
	  PRINTK_INDEX and Clang KCOV also cause explicit errors until native
	  per-callsite printk index records and per-init-function coverage
	  exemptions are implemented. PRINTK=n preserves the native no-output
	  inline semantics without referring to a nonexistent external symbol.
	  With stack protection enabled, this owner currently requires Clang,
	  x86-64 SMP and strong protection without Clang LTO or inline helpers.
	  An empty C translation unit carries the native compiler's configured
	  guard metadata into the Rust bitcode; it defines no runtime code or
	  data. Object, assembly and IR targets verify the same native policy.
